<title>USA: Kansas feedlot cattle trade quiet - USDA.</title>
<headline>Kansas feedlot cattle trade quiet - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>DODGE CITY 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trade was quiet, with no sales slaughter steers or heifers confirmed, USDA said.</p>
<p>Inquiry was moderate and demand light. Sales confirmed for the week to date including late Friday and the weekend on 1,400 head. Asking prices Monday were $65.00 to mostly $66.00, bids $62.00-$63.00. Last sales were Friday at $64.00.</p>
<p>Sales FOB feedlot net weights after four percent shrink. Confirmed: None.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk 312-408-8720))</p>
</text>
